$\begin{align}
h'(x)&=\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[ \dfrac{e^x}{x-1} \right]
\\\\
&=\dfrac{\dfrac{d}{dx}[e^x](x-1)-(e^x)\dfrac{d}{dx}[x-1]}{(x-1)^2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{e^x(x-1)-e^x(1)}{(x-1)^2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{e^x(x-2)}{(x-1)^2}
\end{align}$

Now let's look for $x$-values where $h'$ is zero or undefined.
